[[:db/retract 17592186128569 :answer-field/choices 17592186128570] [:db/retract 17592186128569 :answer-field/choices 17592186128571] [:db/retract 17592186128569 :answer-field/choices 17592186128572] [:db/retract 17592186128569 :answer-field/choices 17592186128573] {:db/id 17592186129848 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,e]\\times [2,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x}-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-2){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{2}^{3}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(e-1)[{y}^{3}]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(e-1)({3}^{3}-{2}^{3}) \\\\  & =19(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1-3x{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A=1-19(e-1)=20-19e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128569 :answer-field/correct "answer-c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6534224-e681-59ea-874f-2267428a83f5" "answer-4a5a35ab-9584-5250-9b05-bab514871947" "answer-216a895e-32d8-5d87-938d-db65b2d1bddc" "answer-c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6534224-e681-59ea-874f-2267428a83f5" :answer/id #uuid "c6534224-e681-59ea-874f-2267428a83f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16+20e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a5a35ab-9584-5250-9b05-bab514871947" :answer/id #uuid "4a5a35ab-9584-5250-9b05-bab514871947" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19-20e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-216a895e-32d8-5d87-938d-db65b2d1bddc" :answer/id #uuid "216a895e-32d8-5d87-938d-db65b2d1bddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19e-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc" :answer/id #uuid "c482d14a-968e-5fba-92dc-75544ab448dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20-19e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a49df285-b000-551a-958c-a18cbfff682c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a49df285-b000-551a-958c-a18cbfff682c" :question/id #uuid "a49df285-b000-551a-958c-a18cbfff682c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80659" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-3,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=5,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}-2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}-2f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =-2\\cdot \\,\\,\\,{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-2\\cdot ({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-3+5) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35e876f8-837f-5088-b5c0-91f0a9d62487"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35e876f8-837f-5088-b5c0-91f0a9d62487" :answer-field/id #uuid "35e876f8-837f-5088-b5c0-91f0a9d62487" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-168581f2-f17c-5d44-a38c-f447560aea9e" :answer-field/ch